---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Clinical Presence | Mood for Life" description="Clinical Presence: a practical framework for staying engaged without burning out.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Forthcoming book</p>
      <h1>Clinical Presence</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical guide to staying engaged, emotionally regulated, and diagnostically clear without burning out.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page can serve publishers, clinicians, podcast hosts, and readers looking for the central idea behind the book.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-card">
      <div class="book-cover-placeholder">Add cover image<br />clinical-presence-cover.jpg</div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid-3">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Attention</h3>
      <p>How clinicians maintain focus amid complexity, time pressure, emotion, and uncertainty.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Regulation</h3>
      <p>How clinicians manage internal reactivity without becoming detached or mechanical.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Judgment</h3>
      <p>How presence supports clearer diagnostic reasoning, rapport, and ethical clinical action.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Working description</h2>
    <p>
      Clinical presence is the disciplined capacity to remain attentive, emotionally regulated, and humanly engaged in the clinical encounter, especially when the patient is distressed, the system is overloaded, or the diagnosis is uncertain.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
